Passes: an optional -O0-only build of PassBuilder (LLVM_ABSD_O0_ONLY)

Failure: none; this is the scout's image-size alternative "O0-only pass
pipeline" (section 4), so the size gate (T3) has a measured image. With
every optimizing pipeline and the textual pass registry in PassBuilder,
all of LLVM's optimization passes are reachable from clang and none is
dropped by --gc-sections.
Change: PassBuilder.cpp includes its registry through
LLVM_PASS_REGISTRY_DEF, which is PassRegistry.def unless LLVM_ABSD_O0_ONLY
is defined, then PassRegistryO0.def (generated by
scripts/llvm-o0-registry.py: the analyses only); under LLVM_ABSD_O0_ONLY,
PassBuilderPipelines.cpp replaces every optimizing pipeline builder with
a fatal error naming it (the per-module default and the two pre-link
builders still hand -O0 to buildO0DefaultPipeline, as upstream does) and
leaves out their helpers; buildO0DefaultPipeline is untouched.
Behaviour preserved: without LLVM_ABSD_O0_ONLY (the normal build, clang-18
and lld) the preprocessed source is identical. The macro is defined only
when scripts/build-llvm-kit.sh compiles these two files a second time for
the clang-o0 and cc1-fe-o0 images; there, -O0 compiles are unchanged and
-O1 and above, -flto and textual pipelines are refused with an error.
Upstreamability: none intended; a measurement configuration.

